WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:04.003
There are 12 of them.

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.526
12 stadiums built in the four corners of Europe.

00:00:10.929 --> 00:00:13.351
Conceived by the most daring architects.

00:00:14.131 --> 00:00:16.652
And built by thousands of workers and engineers.

00:00:20.727 --> 00:00:22.048
12 gigantic arenas,

00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:26.152
selected to host matches for a global event,

00:00:27.132 --> 00:00:29.234
the 2020 European Football Championship.

00:00:31.476 --> 00:00:33.439
Embarking on a unique tour of Europe,

00:00:34.058 --> 00:00:36.561
Discovering the most beautiful stadiums on the continent.

00:01:03.076 --> 00:01:03.898
In this episode,

00:01:05.561 --> 00:01:10.674
the Johan Cruyff Arena in Amsterdam, Netherlands versus the Parken Stadium in Copenhagen, Denmark.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:28.680
On one hand,

00:01:29.262 --> 00:01:30.703
a stadium at a crossroads,

00:01:31.102 --> 00:01:34.545
equipped with a smart lawn and covered with solar panels.

00:01:35.346 --> 00:01:37.947
A global benchmark in sustainable development.

00:01:39.789 --> 00:01:41.750
Our world is constantly changing.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:45.031
We need to understand the major trends,

00:01:45.552 --> 00:01:46.352
We need to adapt to it.

00:01:46.653 --> 00:01:46.992
or better yet,

00:01:47.513 --> 00:01:48.353
anticipate them.

00:01:50.995 --> 00:01:51.495
On the other hand,

00:01:52.055 --> 00:01:54.358
a stadium with retractable stands and roofs,

00:01:54.858 --> 00:01:55.978
fully modular,

00:01:56.319 --> 00:01:57.819
which also host matches,

00:01:57.859 --> 00:01:59.960
concerts rather than office spaces.

00:02:01.742 --> 00:02:04.204
It's great to be in this multifunctional arena.

00:02:04.263 --> 00:02:06.245
The variety of events here,

00:02:06.605 --> 00:02:07.585
It's really special.

00:02:07.786 --> 00:02:08.627
It's unique.

00:02:12.295 --> 00:02:14.139
Amsterdam and Copenhagen,

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.682
two stadiums in northern Europe.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.704
Let's continue our journey to the North Sea coast where Amsterdam is located.

00:02:42.365 --> 00:02:44.266
a city of over 800,000 inhabitants.

00:02:45.508 --> 00:02:48.070
Built entirely on marshland in the 17th century,

00:02:49.352 --> 00:02:54.597
known for its historic center and the canal district, a UNESCO World Heritage Site.

00:02:57.356 --> 00:02:58.436
A very densely populated neighborhood,

00:02:59.397 --> 00:03:03.237
It is impossible for architects to build a stadium in the heart of the historic center.

00:03:05.838 --> 00:03:08.400
Attention then turned towards the southwest of the city,

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.281
in a less populated area,

00:03:10.881 --> 00:03:12.501
next to the Pilsmerbier district.

00:03:14.641 --> 00:03:18.043
This is where the Johan Cruyff Arena now stands.

00:03:27.116 --> 00:03:29.856
Let's return to the name of one of the greatest players in the history of football.

00:03:30.757 --> 00:03:32.837
Three-time Ballon d'Or winner in the 70s.

00:03:34.138 --> 00:03:36.078
A hero for all Dutch people.

00:03:37.639 --> 00:03:38.038
Today,

00:03:38.799 --> 00:03:41.000
The Arena is the home of Ajax Amsterdam.

00:03:41.639 --> 00:03:47.081
The most decorated club in the country and one of the biggest clubs in Europe with 4 Champions League titles to its credit.

00:03:53.122 --> 00:03:55.384
Henk Markerink is the stadium manager.

00:03:56.363 --> 00:03:57.467
Trained as an architect,

00:03:58.009 --> 00:04:02.484
He participated in the design and selection of its location in the early 1990s.

00:04:04.332 --> 00:04:07.213
We looked for an optimal location in terms of infrastructure.

00:04:08.134 --> 00:04:10.855
This place is incredibly well-connected.

00:04:10.895 --> 00:04:14.419
We are south of Amsterdam,

00:04:14.419 --> 00:04:17.120
You could say we're really in the heart of the Netherlands,

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:19.781
very close to the city.

00:04:19.882 --> 00:04:21.163
Its location is perfect.

00:04:21.802 --> 00:04:22.523
We have the trains,

00:04:22.824 --> 00:04:23.423
the subways,

00:04:23.564 --> 00:04:23.983
the buses,

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.805
and even the highways that pass through here.

00:04:26.185 --> 00:04:28.846
So it's very easy to access for cars too.

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.873
The stadium is indeed located on the A2 motorway.

00:04:36.933 --> 00:04:42.335
A major route that crosses the entire country to transport supporters by car from major urban centers.

00:04:43.055 --> 00:04:43.675
Maastricht,

00:04:44.055 --> 00:04:45.716
Eindhoven or Trescht.

00:04:47.456 --> 00:04:48.377
In 20 minutes by subway,

00:04:49.037 --> 00:04:51.377
The stadium can be reached from the centre of Amsterdam.

00:04:53.598 --> 00:04:58.780
And a whole network of buses makes it easy to access the arena from the surrounding suburbs.

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.199
But for the Amsterdam city council,

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:06.842
Building a stadium in this location was also strategic for a completely different reason.

00:05:10.602 --> 00:05:12.383
The neighborhood was very disadvantaged,

00:05:12.943 --> 00:05:14.624
There was a very high unemployment rate.

00:05:14.684 --> 00:05:18.244
Together with city officials,

00:05:18.545 --> 00:05:19.245
we said to ourselves,

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:21.285
if we build the stadium here,

00:05:21.884 --> 00:05:24.045
We are going to give investment a boost.

00:05:24.506 --> 00:05:26.247
And that will revitalize the whole neighborhood.

00:05:27.388 --> 00:05:27.749
Today,

00:05:27.789 --> 00:05:30.050
It's not just the stadium that has been built here.

00:05:30.591 --> 00:05:32.993
There is a whole range of sports facilities,

00:05:32.994 --> 00:05:33.673
leisure activities

00:05:34.114 --> 00:05:36.475
entertainment options have skyrocketed,

00:05:36.956 --> 00:05:37.756
like the rest of the neighborhood.

00:05:39.718 --> 00:05:43.301
We may not have solved all the problems by building this stadium,

00:05:44.141 --> 00:05:51.727
but the subsequent economic upturn has allowed the entire area to prosper since 1996.

00:05:53.115 --> 00:05:54.156
In 1993,

00:05:54.617 --> 00:05:56.781
Then began one of the biggest construction projects in the Netherlands.

00:05:57.781 --> 00:05:58.423
Architects,

00:05:58.543 --> 00:06:04.250
Engineers and workers will work for three years to build the largest stadium in the country.

00:06:05.692 --> 00:06:08.616
But the first difficulties appear with the first stroke of the bulldozer.

00:06:10.944 --> 00:06:12.105
This used to be a lake here.

00:06:12.365 --> 00:06:13.708
so a marshy area.

00:06:13.908 --> 00:06:15.209
The ground was very unstable.

00:06:17.232 --> 00:06:19.834
To erect a stadium weighing tens of thousands of tons,

00:06:20.375 --> 00:06:26.083
The architects had to draw inspiration from methods used by their ancestors to build the houses in the historic center of Amsterdam.

00:06:26.903 --> 00:06:29.266
Houses built entirely on stilts.

00:06:32.668 --> 00:06:34.590
The idea is then to reproduce the same principle.

00:06:35.511 --> 00:06:36.591
To ensure the foundations,

00:06:37.252 --> 00:06:45.221
The engineers had the holes dug in the unstable soil made of peat and clay until they reached a layer of dense sand located 16 meters deep.

00:06:46.242 --> 00:06:46.841
In each hole,

00:06:47.603 --> 00:06:51.387
The workers lowered huge steel structures down to the layer of sand.

00:06:55.415 --> 00:07:01.218
Concrete was poured to fill the holes and to provide enough pillars to support the entire stadium.

00:07:02.899 --> 00:07:03.379
In total,

00:07:04.019 --> 00:07:08.040
The Johan Cruyff Arena rests on 2000 pillars, each 16 meters long.

00:07:08.461 --> 00:07:10.281
45 centimeters in diameter.

00:07:18.816 --> 00:07:19.917
With the foundations completed,

00:07:20.538 --> 00:07:25.944
The workers were able to begin construction of the stadium, taking into account an original element from the design stage.

00:07:26.605 --> 00:07:27.727
the presence of a road.

00:07:29.609 --> 00:07:30.569
For architects,

00:07:31.271 --> 00:07:34.694
A solution had to be found to fit a road in the same place.

00:07:35.096 --> 00:07:37.338
a huge car park and a stadium.

00:07:40.713 --> 00:07:42.574
The road was already under construction.

00:07:43.574 --> 00:07:45.015
But it gave us an advantage.

00:07:46.216 --> 00:07:47.497
Since there was a road,

00:07:47.857 --> 00:07:50.999
the land was cheaper and it could be used for several things.

00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:52.741
If we were to lift the road,

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.882
We could build a car park underneath.

00:07:55.602 --> 00:07:56.223
At the end of the day,

00:07:56.543 --> 00:08:00.608
We modified our plans and envisioned three buildings stacked one on top of the other.

00:08:00.908 --> 00:08:01.429
a tunnel,

00:08:01.509 --> 00:08:02.550
a car park and a stadium.

00:08:03.011 --> 00:08:05.153
And that's what we built.

00:08:06.675 --> 00:08:09.819
A first car park with 2500 spaces was therefore built.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:10.961
above the foundations.

00:08:12.202 --> 00:08:14.663
Then the road was raised to the next level.

00:08:17.165 --> 00:08:18.446
On either side of this road,

00:08:19.106 --> 00:08:23.749
A second level of parking has been created so that visitors can access the stands directly.

00:08:25.109 --> 00:08:25.590
In the end,

00:08:26.311 --> 00:08:32.179
The football pitch and the stadium rest entirely on these two levels of parking, through which the tunnel passes.

00:08:33.081 --> 00:08:33.761
During matches,

00:08:34.322 --> 00:08:38.028
The players move around on the pitch with cars driving just below.

00:08:48.043 --> 00:08:48.984
By stacking the road,

00:08:49.084 --> 00:08:50.245
the car park and the stadium,

00:08:50.886 --> 00:08:57.472
The architects have achieved the feat of occupying the minimum amount of space in the same area to accommodate the maximum number of visitors.

00:08:57.473 --> 00:09:03.598
1996,

00:09:04.179 --> 00:09:07.602
The company BAM also participated in the construction of the stadium.

00:09:14.015 --> 00:09:18.697
There are several reasons that led them to build a road under the stadium.

00:09:18.977 --> 00:09:19.438
First of all,

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:21.699
The city wanted to turn this stadium into a monument.

00:09:21.819 --> 00:09:24.940
And the best way to showcase a building,

00:09:24.942 --> 00:09:26.062
It's about raising it up.

00:09:26.062 --> 00:09:27.201
Afterwards,

00:09:27.202 --> 00:09:28.242
A parking lot was needed.

00:09:28.502 --> 00:09:32.225
If we were to raise the stadium and build a car park underneath,

00:09:32.225 --> 00:09:36.626
This allowed two things to be built on the same ground footprint.

00:09:36.627 --> 00:09:38.226
And then,

00:09:38.346 --> 00:09:39.567
always to save space,

00:09:39.828 --> 00:09:42.251
They built a road that goes through the stadium.

00:09:42.252 --> 00:09:42.851
So,

00:09:43.232 --> 00:09:45.174
thanks to this road,

00:09:45.294 --> 00:09:48.857
We always had access to the area behind the stadium,

00:09:48.858 --> 00:09:51.440
but also to all parking lots.

00:09:52.461 --> 00:09:58.127
So I really think that's the winning combination they used to build the road and the stadium together.

00:10:04.215 --> 00:10:09.577
The Johan Cruyff Arena is now one of those large stadiums built on the outskirts of urban areas.

00:10:12.158 --> 00:10:12.558
London,

00:10:13.319 --> 00:10:13.739
Glasgow,

00:10:14.279 --> 00:10:18.561
Saint Petersburg has all established its football temple away from the city centre.

00:10:20.982 --> 00:10:22.442
Others made a different choice.

00:10:27.084 --> 00:10:27.844
In Copenhagen,

00:10:28.344 --> 00:10:29.384
capital of Denmark,

00:10:30.085 --> 00:10:32.466
Fans can travel to the match by bicycle.

00:10:34.485 --> 00:10:37.627
Parken Stadium is located in the residential area of ​​Lostorne.

00:10:38.567 --> 00:10:40.528
a stone's throw from the historic heart of Copenhagen.

00:10:44.869 --> 00:10:50.050
This stadium, renovated in the 1990s, is located on the site of Copenhagen's former sports park.

00:10:50.529 --> 00:10:51.671
over a century old.

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:54.331
A legendary place for all Danes.

00:10:57.259 --> 00:11:01.282
Tom Danielson worked at the architectural firm that originally designed the renovation.

00:11:02.222 --> 00:11:02.543
For him,

00:11:02.803 --> 00:11:03.343
No doubt about it.

00:11:03.984 --> 00:11:07.226
the stadium was to be rebuilt in the same location as the old one.

00:11:12.509 --> 00:11:17.333
Various organizations have begun searching for a new location for a new national arena.

00:11:18.695 --> 00:11:23.979
Several locations in the vicinity of Copenhagen have been studied.

00:11:24.458 --> 00:11:30.104
It was a close call that a new national stadium wasn't built in Brombe.

00:11:31.485 --> 00:11:32.105
But fortunately,

00:11:32.105 --> 00:11:32.524
I would say,

00:11:32.846 --> 00:11:36.788
And I believe that all the inhabitants of Copenhagen and all Danes would agree with me.

00:11:37.229 --> 00:11:41.211
We finally managed to establish that it had to be here.

00:11:41.703 --> 00:11:44.548
That's where history lies,

00:11:44.687 --> 00:11:50.535
that is to say, at the site where the old Copenhagen athletics stadium had stood since 1912,

00:11:50.676 --> 00:11:57.044
and where some of the very first football matches in Danish history were played.

00:11:59.711 --> 00:12:01.132
At the turn of the 1990s,

00:12:01.693 --> 00:12:03.735
The architects had to overcome a major challenge.

00:12:04.535 --> 00:12:09.039
How can a new 38,000-seat stadium be built in an area that is already developed?

00:12:13.103 --> 00:12:13.983
Before its renovation,

00:12:14.504 --> 00:12:17.307
Parken Stadium measured approximately 100 meters by 60 meters.

00:12:18.727 --> 00:12:22.410
The proposed new stadium has a footprint of 200 meters by 165 meters.

00:12:24.012 --> 00:12:26.414
It is unthinkable to encroach on Fallet Parken.

00:12:28.295 --> 00:12:31.557
It was impossible to destroy the hockey pitch, which was so precious to the Danes.

00:12:32.399 --> 00:12:32.878
The only option,

00:12:33.498 --> 00:12:35.399
rotate the stadium 90°.

00:12:38.301 --> 00:12:44.625
The local football club B93 agrees to give up its training ground to accommodate the new national stadium.

00:12:45.746 --> 00:12:47.767
The location is therefore perfectly suited.

00:12:48.867 --> 00:12:53.250
The new footprint helps to preserve the famous residential area of ​​Pomp-le-Villiers.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.301
Once the orientation of the new stadium has been decided,

00:12:57.961 --> 00:13:01.802
The architects and engineers demolished almost the entire old stadium.

00:13:02.443 --> 00:13:04.603
with the exception of the long main stand,

00:13:05.044 --> 00:13:06.644
which then becomes a short platform.

00:13:09.785 --> 00:13:11.286
Three new stands have been added.

00:13:12.386 --> 00:13:16.428
Two parallel to the Astorale and a third opposite the old stand.

00:13:19.788 --> 00:13:21.308
But the architects don't stop there.

00:13:21.968 --> 00:13:23.971
They were taking a bold gamble for the time.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:26.371
Adding offices to a stadium.

00:13:27.932 --> 00:13:38.399
Three buildings were then constructed around the tribes.

00:13:49.365 --> 00:13:51.767
The water stadium was built in 1992.

00:13:52.106 --> 00:13:53.707
There were just three stands.

00:13:55.008 --> 00:13:57.349
Since we did not own the property at the time,

00:13:57.749 --> 00:13:59.028
We had no control.

00:13:59.549 --> 00:14:00.970
nor on architecture,

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:02.770
nor on the stadium's infrastructure.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:07.851
There was indeed the old main stand,

00:14:08.253 --> 00:14:09.432
the one that had been preserved,

00:14:10.273 --> 00:14:11.453
but it was old,

00:14:11.813 --> 00:14:15.174
The concrete was in poor condition, as were the attached infrastructures.

00:14:15.794 --> 00:14:17.176
clearly insufficient.

00:14:19.467 --> 00:14:20.087
In 2009,

00:14:20.788 --> 00:14:21.848
FC Copenhagen,

00:14:22.008 --> 00:14:23.509
now the owner of the stadium,

00:14:23.949 --> 00:14:30.093
they finally had the old stand dating from 1955 demolished and replaced it with a smaller stand.

00:14:31.254 --> 00:14:32.154
At the rear of the stands,

00:14:32.574 --> 00:14:33.515
running along the entire length of the field,

00:14:34.115 --> 00:14:36.416
A huge office building for rent is being constructed.

00:14:37.357 --> 00:14:40.178
This will make the stadium profitable outside of football matches.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:42.801
On normal days,

00:14:43.062 --> 00:14:45.163
when there is no match,

00:14:45.244 --> 00:14:46.706
The stadium is still alive, though.

00:14:46.826 --> 00:14:49.448
You meet a lot of people here.

00:14:49.528 --> 00:14:49.948
Actually,

00:14:50.009 --> 00:14:51.850
400 people work in our offices,

00:14:52.351 --> 00:14:55.335
in all sorts of very different businesses.

00:14:55.774 --> 00:14:56.755
There is a private hospital,

00:14:57.236 --> 00:14:58.077
sports clubs,

00:14:59.458 --> 00:14:59.879
a bodysuit...

00:15:00.139 --> 00:15:03.802
SDS, which is a kind of therapeutic center,

00:15:03.861 --> 00:15:05.743
all the ingredients for a business location.

00:15:07.384 --> 00:15:11.706
We also have a 3-star restaurant in the Gile Michelin guide called Geranium.

00:15:13.606 --> 00:15:14.768
Working here every day,

00:15:15.008 --> 00:15:16.129
even when there is no match,

00:15:17.009 --> 00:15:17.769
It makes him feel alive.

00:15:17.889 --> 00:15:19.291
It gives him a unique energy.

00:15:20.211 --> 00:15:21.511
It's a fantastic feeling.

00:15:22.831 --> 00:15:27.475
Making a stadium profitable outside of football matches has become one of the priorities for managers.

00:15:37.268 --> 00:15:39.470
Since its creation in 1996,

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:43.452
The Johan Cruyff Arena was also designed with this in mind.

00:15:44.432 --> 00:15:47.014
It hosts numerous events throughout the year.

00:15:58.919 --> 00:16:00.181
If we only had football,

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.181
We could not be profitable.

00:16:03.461 --> 00:16:04.042
From the very beginning,

00:16:04.542 --> 00:16:07.023
The stadium was designed to be multifunctional.

00:16:10.143 --> 00:16:13.303
Ajax and the national team remain the foundation of our business.

00:16:13.403 --> 00:16:14.824
But besides that,

00:16:15.625 --> 00:16:16.605
There are concerts,

00:16:16.644 --> 00:16:17.465
major events

00:16:17.505 --> 00:16:18.145
conferences,

00:16:18.265 --> 00:16:19.045
seminars.

00:16:21.187 --> 00:16:22.886
The stadium is operating at full capacity.

00:16:22.986 --> 00:16:23.787
7 days a week,

00:16:24.086 --> 00:16:25.408
24 hours a day.

00:16:28.311 --> 00:16:32.873
The Johan Cruyff Arena has thus become the essential concert venue for an entire country.

00:16:34.213 --> 00:16:35.954
The world's biggest bands have performed there.

00:16:36.894 --> 00:16:38.015
From U2 to Bon Jovi,

00:16:38.455 --> 00:16:39.796
including the Rolling Stones.

00:16:43.477 --> 00:16:44.858
But as the years went by,

00:16:45.399 --> 00:16:47.359
The stadium has become a victim of its own success.

00:16:51.908 --> 00:16:54.211
Ajax attracted huge crowds of spectators,

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:55.831
much more than we had anticipated.

00:16:57.573 --> 00:17:01.756
We were also able to organize many more concerts and events than we had anticipated.

00:17:03.399 --> 00:17:08.923
That's when we realized that our facilities were insufficient for the number of people we were receiving.

00:17:11.045 --> 00:17:12.646
We were seriously lacking in equipment,

00:17:13.226 --> 00:17:13.947
of restaurants,

00:17:13.988 --> 00:17:14.707
refreshment stands,

00:17:14.768 --> 00:17:15.408
toilets,

00:17:15.788 --> 00:17:15.989
Short,

00:17:16.309 --> 00:17:17.411
of a whole bunch of things.

00:17:20.407 --> 00:17:21.229
Over the years,

00:17:21.808 --> 00:17:23.711
The stadium is undergoing numerous renovations.

00:17:24.771 --> 00:17:27.773
Escalators and elevators to facilitate access to the stadium.

00:17:29.194 --> 00:17:30.855
The expansion of certain spaces.

00:17:32.597 --> 00:17:33.898
But that's still not enough.

00:17:35.039 --> 00:17:39.884
The stadium needs to think bigger in order to increase services and public capacity.

00:17:41.539 --> 00:17:42.401
For architects,

00:17:42.540 --> 00:17:43.422
This is a new challenge.

00:17:44.563 --> 00:17:48.905
How can a stadium be significantly enlarged without drastically altering the existing structure?

00:17:51.828 --> 00:17:57.314
The option chosen is to add a new steel structure that fits against the old stadium walls.

00:17:58.494 --> 00:18:02.038
A kind of immense, multi-level metal cage attached to the stadium.

00:18:04.695 --> 00:18:06.355
To support this steel structure,

00:18:07.096 --> 00:18:11.478
New foundations are being created and the stadium's old load-bearing columns are being reinforced.

00:18:15.519 --> 00:18:16.638
In its widest part,

00:18:17.019 --> 00:18:19.740
The cage has two floors, each over 80 meters long.

00:18:20.579 --> 00:18:23.961
enough to easily accommodate the 7000 supporters in the stand.

00:18:27.961 --> 00:18:29.603
And to isolate the cage from the outside,

00:18:30.182 --> 00:18:33.104
The architects chose a material that has already proven its worth.

00:18:38.859 --> 00:18:40.421
We wanted to create a lot of light,

00:18:40.641 --> 00:18:41.321
Plenty of space.

00:18:41.942 --> 00:18:43.743
To succeed in creating such a large facade,

00:18:44.163 --> 00:18:48.166
We chose a lightweight material in order to reduce the overall mass as much as possible.

00:18:48.866 --> 00:18:52.288
We therefore opted for an ETFE cushion structure.

00:18:53.289 --> 00:18:55.011
This provides transparency in certain areas.

00:18:55.411 --> 00:18:57.273
Other parts are merely translucent.

00:18:57.733 --> 00:18:59.415
You can still see through it.

00:19:00.116 --> 00:19:04.220
And the enclosure is only partially insulated.

00:19:06.562 --> 00:19:07.963
After a year and a half of work,

00:19:08.704 --> 00:19:10.505
The east side of the stadium is finished.

00:19:11.466 --> 00:19:14.470
But future extension work is planned on the other sides.

00:19:17.771 --> 00:19:18.532
In a few years,

00:19:19.094 --> 00:19:26.261
The Johan Cruyff Arena will have a much more rounded silhouette to accommodate more people and offer even more services.

00:19:40.365 --> 00:19:46.868
Parken Stadium also began its transformation phase in the 2000s to bring new experiences to the public.

00:19:48.009 --> 00:19:51.371
The first major change was the construction of a retractable roof.

00:20:00.923 --> 00:20:04.307
The retractable roof was built in 2001.

00:20:04.307 --> 00:20:08.990
simply because the Olsen brothers won Eurovision the previous year.

00:20:09.010 --> 00:20:12.113
You should know that when your country wins Eurovision,

00:20:12.232 --> 00:20:13.875
He welcomed him the following year.

00:20:13.954 --> 00:20:16.356
This is a huge opportunity to welcome

00:20:16.757 --> 00:20:19.179
30,000 people for the Eurovision final.

00:20:23.482 --> 00:20:24.042
At the time,

00:20:24.624 --> 00:20:27.605
only a few stadiums in the world are equipped with retractable roofs.

00:20:33.894 --> 00:20:39.317
These are huge steel and glass panels that slide over each other to open and close.

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:50.826
Far too expensive for the Parken Stadium managers who ended up choosing a flexible roof supported by a series of steel frames.

00:20:52.326 --> 00:20:55.688
Lars Ostenfeld Riemann supervised the construction of the roof.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:58.431
He takes us up to a height of 35 meters.

00:21:05.789 --> 00:21:18.013
We are here on the fixed part of the roof where we have installed this large beam along the entire length of the roof, under which is the travel rail.

00:21:18.073 --> 00:21:25.915
This installation supports the motors but also all the inlet beams that span the entire width of the roof and allow it to be closed.

00:21:27.116 --> 00:21:28.396
And it is precisely these engines

00:21:28.675 --> 00:21:33.279
thanks to a system of gears that will advance and move the crossbeams.

00:21:33.539 --> 00:21:34.280
You can see it clearly here.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:39.045
The engine moves forward thanks to the rack and pinion, and once it has reached its final position,

00:21:40.687 --> 00:21:44.309
We lower this piston and then,

00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:47.293
We are certain that the system can no longer move.

00:21:51.563 --> 00:21:52.043
In total,

00:21:52.763 --> 00:21:55.444
The roof of the Stadparken is equipped with 26 motors.

00:21:55.824 --> 00:21:59.645
each positioned at the end of the 13 steel beams that span the stadium.

00:22:02.906 --> 00:22:05.967
26 motors that must move at a constant speed,

00:22:06.427 --> 00:22:07.327
guided by rails.

00:22:07.347 --> 00:22:14.710
If one engine runs faster than another,

00:22:14.711 --> 00:22:19.971
one of the steel beams may suddenly become deflected.

00:22:20.652 --> 00:22:24.935
This is a huge risk because not only are the beams no longer parallel,

00:22:24.955 --> 00:22:28.778
but this also generates a lot of force and movement within the system.

00:22:28.958 --> 00:22:33.242
which is very bad for the entire structure.

00:22:35.804 --> 00:22:36.985
To avoid disaster,

00:22:37.547 --> 00:22:42.290
Each motor and each beam is equipped with sensors that measure their movements in real time.

00:22:44.519 --> 00:22:48.124
Two people on each side of the roof monitor the smooth progress of the process.

00:22:49.085 --> 00:22:49.945
At the slightest problem,

00:22:50.405 --> 00:22:51.866
They can stop the roof's movement.

00:22:57.873 --> 00:22:59.794
But before proceeding to close the roof,

00:23:00.414 --> 00:23:02.778
The technicians must perform another maneuver.

00:23:03.577 --> 00:23:08.522
Because supporting a roof weighing several hundred tons was not planned for the old stadium structure.

00:23:14.645 --> 00:23:22.712
Installing a roof over the existing structure was really very difficult.

00:23:24.074 --> 00:23:27.537
The original roof already housed some of the grandstand seating.

00:23:28.497 --> 00:23:31.860
but these structures could not support an entire new roof.

00:23:32.381 --> 00:23:39.226
So we were forced to reinforce the existing roof in many places.

00:23:43.083 --> 00:23:48.366
The engineers therefore had to think of a way to reinforce the two enormous steel side beams.

00:23:58.311 --> 00:24:01.473
They designed two pivoting columns in the center of each one.

00:24:05.535 --> 00:24:06.936
When the stadium is open-air,

00:24:07.476 --> 00:24:10.318
The columns are folded and suspended under the existing roof.

00:24:16.704 --> 00:24:17.745
Before the roof is closed,

00:24:18.326 --> 00:24:22.509
The first thing to do is to rotate the columns and fix them securely to the ground.

00:24:37.817 --> 00:24:38.136
When

00:24:38.196 --> 00:24:38.937
Everything is in place.

00:24:39.657 --> 00:24:41.378
The roof can begin to close.

00:24:55.778 --> 00:24:58.539
In order to minimize the load on the stands,

00:24:59.180 --> 00:25:00.000
the 13 beams of the...

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.601
The roofs are connected to each other by PVC membranes.

00:25:04.281 --> 00:25:04.903
These membranes,

00:25:05.002 --> 00:25:06.343
made up of several layers,

00:25:06.784 --> 00:25:09.424
are successively inflated with pressurized air,

00:25:09.904 --> 00:25:12.086
in order to stiffen the entire roof structure.

00:25:18.750 --> 00:25:19.691
To fold down the roof,

00:25:20.330 --> 00:25:21.811
The air pumps are switched off.

00:25:23.393 --> 00:25:24.653
The membranes deflate,

00:25:25.394 --> 00:25:27.674
The beams are placed close together.

00:25:30.039 --> 00:25:33.122
The PVC membranes hang like curtains between each beam.

00:25:34.982 --> 00:25:38.184
The assembly will then slide under the rigid roof of stand D.

00:25:54.894 --> 00:25:55.194
Grace

00:25:55.195 --> 00:25:56.155
with a retractable roof...

00:25:56.615 --> 00:26:00.760
Parken Stadium has been able to host the biggest sporting and musical events in the country.

00:26:03.483 --> 00:26:05.066
A few years ago,

00:26:05.125 --> 00:26:07.009
The band Coldplay used to perform here.

00:26:07.710 --> 00:26:10.272
One hour before the doors open,

00:26:10.432 --> 00:26:15.358
when the musicians were doing their soundcheck and the spectators were queuing outside,

00:26:16.949 --> 00:26:17.789
Chris Martin,

00:26:17.829 --> 00:26:18.630
the band's singer,

00:26:18.651 --> 00:26:21.173
came to see us at the office and told us

00:26:21.875 --> 00:26:24.116
"I can't play in the rain."

00:26:24.176 --> 00:26:26.860
It's too difficult for me and it's a real shame for the audience.

00:26:27.320 --> 00:26:29.123
It's going to ruin the whole atmosphere of the concert.

00:26:29.703 --> 00:26:31.605
Can you close the roof?

00:26:35.065 --> 00:26:37.145
Everyone remained silent.

00:26:37.265 --> 00:26:38.866
No one wanted to answer that question.

00:26:40.028 --> 00:26:40.727
In barely an hour,

00:26:40.989 --> 00:26:42.950
This meant bringing in the technicians,

00:26:43.690 --> 00:26:46.972
to install everything and then deploy the roof.

00:26:48.693 --> 00:26:49.033
That's a sign...

00:26:49.294 --> 00:26:50.496
Life has turned everything upside down, actually.

00:26:50.675 --> 00:26:52.597
Eventually,

00:26:52.637 --> 00:26:56.082
We quickly organized a production meeting and everyone said,

00:26:56.623 --> 00:26:56.962
Let's do it.

00:26:57.443 --> 00:26:58.365
Let's deploy the roof.

00:26:58.766 --> 00:27:00.827
We postponed the concert by one hour.

00:27:00.867 --> 00:27:03.151
But Coldplay was able to play.

00:27:04.652 --> 00:27:05.753
Chris Martin was delighted.

00:27:06.192 --> 00:27:07.394
We all received a badge that said "Love".

00:27:07.814 --> 00:27:09.935
on top and everyone was very happy.

00:27:11.997 --> 00:27:17.420
Parken Stadium also has a major advantage in hosting concerts and shows within its grounds.

00:27:18.240 --> 00:27:19.521
a retractable grandstand.

00:27:25.183 --> 00:27:26.085
80 meters long,

00:27:27.025 --> 00:27:30.647
It was the largest mobile grandstand in all of Scandinavia at the time of its construction.

00:27:32.923 --> 00:27:35.446
Michael Jensen is the stadium's technical director.

00:27:36.449 --> 00:27:37.470
With each manipulation,

00:27:37.931 --> 00:27:40.453
He is there to oversee the smooth running of operations.

00:27:50.528 --> 00:27:52.389
When the new grandstand was built,

00:27:52.788 --> 00:27:56.290
We needed space downstairs to build the stage when there are concerts.

00:27:57.330 --> 00:27:57.591
Before,

00:27:58.031 --> 00:28:00.732
We had a mobile scaffold on which we placed seats,

00:28:01.092 --> 00:28:03.052
and it took about a week to assemble.

00:28:03.132 --> 00:28:05.273
and it also took a week to dismantle afterwards.

00:28:05.932 --> 00:28:08.814
So that's why we had a mobile grandstand built.

00:28:09.153 --> 00:28:11.855
to be able to switch quickly between concerts and football matches.

00:28:21.932 --> 00:28:22.613
40 minutes,

00:28:23.293 --> 00:28:28.417
Michael and his colleagues can fit in the 3900 seats supported by the steel structures of the grandstand.

00:28:29.999 --> 00:28:34.142
The bleachers move thanks to an ingenious system devised by the injectors.

00:28:36.544 --> 00:28:39.586
Each row of seats is supported by a steel structure.

00:28:41.088 --> 00:28:45.951
These structures are built in such a way as to fit together according to a collision system.

00:28:47.733 --> 00:28:49.815
The entire stand is divided into 8 sections.

00:28:52.152 --> 00:28:54.533
Each section is set in motion by means of a motor.

00:28:56.653 --> 00:28:57.394
Once activated,

00:28:58.095 --> 00:29:02.257
Each motor winds a steel chain which pulls the lower row of the grandstand.

00:29:05.358 --> 00:29:09.740
The movement of the lower row then in turn affects all the seats above it.

00:29:11.421 --> 00:29:14.502
The structures beneath the stands then fit together, one under the other.

00:29:15.303 --> 00:29:17.123
freeing up space in front of the stands.

00:29:21.751 --> 00:29:22.993
With each movement from the stands,

00:29:23.555 --> 00:29:27.102
Michael and his colleagues systematically monitor what is happening under the stands.

00:29:34.308 --> 00:29:38.029
A few of us go underneath to take care of the various security procedures.

00:29:38.730 --> 00:29:40.510
because it is deployed in three stages.

00:29:41.251 --> 00:29:42.112
And at each stage,

00:29:42.711 --> 00:29:46.574
We check if everything is in place and properly aligned.

00:29:46.614 --> 00:29:48.315
We mustn't let things go off the rails.

00:29:49.355 --> 00:29:51.615
It would be catastrophic if it moved at an angle.

00:29:52.096 --> 00:29:54.017
because it would be very difficult to put it back straight.

00:29:54.237 --> 00:29:54.597
So that,

00:29:54.978 --> 00:29:57.298
This is a procedure that requires a lot of attention from us.

00:30:01.572 --> 00:30:02.294
Once stacked,

00:30:02.876 --> 00:30:06.105
The 19 rows of seats form a wall more than 6 meters high.

00:30:10.367 --> 00:30:13.028
The space freed up allows for the installation of the stage for the artists.

00:30:14.048 --> 00:30:15.750
And for easy access to behind-the-scenes areas,

00:30:16.230 --> 00:30:18.470
the stand needs to undergo a second transformation.

00:30:20.790 --> 00:30:26.732
The mobile grandstand we have here gives us the advantage of being able to move the middle section out when we have concerts.

00:30:26.952 --> 00:30:28.192
And that gives us enormous advantages.

00:30:28.992 --> 00:30:33.534
Because when you remove the middle section and build the scene in front,

00:30:33.574 --> 00:30:36.055
We can bring all the equipment directly onto the stage.

00:30:39.788 --> 00:30:41.631
To create this hole in the mobile grandstand,

00:30:42.252 --> 00:30:45.636
Mickaël and his team have to remove more than 150 seats at a time.

00:30:46.197 --> 00:30:49.041
that is the equivalent of 5 tonnes to be moved by forklift.

00:30:52.288 --> 00:30:57.052
Seats are also being removed from each stand to create access routes and emergency exits.

00:30:58.193 --> 00:30:59.334
Two exits from stand C,

00:31:00.054 --> 00:31:03.157
two others in stand B and one exit in stand A.

00:31:04.418 --> 00:31:04.898
In the end,

00:31:05.459 --> 00:31:10.743
Parken Stadium is transformed into a huge arena ready to welcome the public for major events.

00:31:14.507 --> 00:31:16.613
And to improve the acoustics during concerts,

00:31:17.154 --> 00:31:21.747
Huge woolen drapes are unfurled under the roof and along the buildings surrounding the stage.

00:31:27.935 --> 00:31:30.239
During the concerts,

00:31:30.278 --> 00:31:37.547
Curtains are always installed on office towers because they are made of glass and sound reverberates off the glass.

00:31:37.707 --> 00:31:41.691
It creates an echo and gives us very bad acoustics.

00:31:41.931 --> 00:31:43.553
With these thick LED curtains,

00:31:43.732 --> 00:31:45.055
the sound is immediately muffled.

00:31:45.535 --> 00:31:48.739
This makes the acoustics of the stadium excellent.

00:31:50.687 --> 00:31:51.628
At each concert,

00:31:52.170 --> 00:31:54.413
Thousands of fans gather on the football pitch.

00:31:55.213 --> 00:31:57.196
Enough to destroy the lawn in a few hours.

00:31:58.259 --> 00:31:59.440
To avoid damaging the grass,

00:31:59.880 --> 00:32:02.825
Mickaël and his teams use very efficient equipment.

00:32:05.607 --> 00:32:07.449
To protect the lawn,

00:32:07.451 --> 00:32:10.091
which is our sacred ground here in the stadium,

00:32:10.413 --> 00:32:13.434
These large panels are installed on top of the grass.

00:32:13.454 --> 00:32:19.500
This will become the floor to accommodate all the audience members who come to see the concert and remain standing.

00:32:19.600 --> 00:32:23.384
The plates are very thick.

00:32:24.264 --> 00:32:26.646
They protect the lawn from trampling.

00:32:26.706 --> 00:32:30.630
but there are also holes to allow air to circulate and the grass to breathe.

00:32:35.599 --> 00:32:37.000
On the surface of each panel,

00:32:37.601 --> 00:32:42.105
Dozens of aligned holes were drilled to allow air to circulate at grass level.

00:32:44.927 --> 00:32:46.888
Spilled liquids do not pass through the holes.

00:32:47.529 --> 00:32:49.731
They are collected in channels carved into the panel.

00:32:54.295 --> 00:32:57.117
On the underside of the panel in contact with the lawn,

00:32:57.577 --> 00:33:00.000
Circular feet slightly raise the panel,

00:33:00.520 --> 00:33:02.501
which allows for a better distribution of the workload.

00:33:06.775 --> 00:33:11.899
Each one square meter panel weighs 12 kilos and is easily handled by two people.

00:33:13.881 --> 00:33:18.245
However, six hours are needed to completely cover the stadium's lawn by heart.

00:33:26.732 --> 00:33:29.174
If these panels protect the grass from public trampling,

00:33:29.914 --> 00:33:33.737
They were also designed to allow grass to grow even once covered.

00:33:38.755 --> 00:33:47.398
The 60 mm thick panel has cavities on its underside that allow air to circulate and provide enough space for grass to grow.

00:33:51.439 --> 00:33:52.059
The material,

00:33:52.600 --> 00:33:54.721
high-density polyethylene plastic,

00:33:55.180 --> 00:33:56.581
is naturally translucent.

00:33:57.281 --> 00:34:00.902
It therefore allows light to pass through and does not stop the process of photosynthesis.

00:34:03.735 --> 00:34:07.338
The solar radiation that passes through the panel removes the water contained in the soil.

00:34:10.942 --> 00:34:13.384
A cloud of vapor then forms under each cavity.

00:34:16.025 --> 00:34:21.549
The moisture eventually condenses under the droplet, and drops then fall onto the grass.

00:34:22.530 --> 00:34:24.432
providing the water necessary for its survival.

00:34:26.333 --> 00:34:30.217
Therefore, the lawn does not need to be watered when it is covered by the panels.

00:34:36.903 --> 00:34:40.407
We can host concerts that are organized very quickly.

00:34:40.427 --> 00:34:44.389
with very quick installation and uninstallation.

00:34:45.190 --> 00:34:48.311
The panels covering the lawn were removed, and a few hours later,

00:34:48.352 --> 00:34:50.492
There's a football match taking place here.

00:34:50.594 --> 00:34:54.856
But the panels cannot be left on the grass for more than 72 consecutive hours.

00:34:54.856 --> 00:34:55.916
no more than 3 days.

00:34:56.538 --> 00:34:56.818
Otherwise,

00:34:56.898 --> 00:34:59.239
The grass will rise with air.

00:34:59.480 --> 00:35:00.000
water, and especially water.

00:35:01.201 --> 00:35:02.161
of light.

00:35:02.242 --> 00:35:03.682
It may turn yellow.

00:35:03.684 --> 00:35:04.884
to brown,

00:35:04.885 --> 00:35:07.266
to lose its beautiful green color.

00:35:08.407 --> 00:35:14.733
Playing a football match after a concert is therefore not always the ideal solution for keeping a pitch in perfect condition.

00:35:22.500 --> 00:35:23.021
Amsterdam,

00:35:23.682 --> 00:35:26.826
The managers of the Johan Cruyff Arena made a completely different choice.

00:35:27.987 --> 00:35:31.833
They opted for a complete change of the turf after the concert season.

00:35:40.451 --> 00:35:41.572
Under normal circumstances,

00:35:41.592 --> 00:35:44.474
We have a season of festivals and concerts.

00:35:44.534 --> 00:35:46.675
It starts at the end of the league matches,

00:35:46.795 --> 00:35:47.476
So around mid-May,

00:35:47.477 --> 00:35:51.438
And it ends in May.

00:35:51.719 --> 00:35:53.179
That represents two and a half months.

00:35:53.300 --> 00:35:55.021
almost three months for the concerts.

00:35:57.663 --> 00:36:00.364
That's far too long a period for a covered lawn.

00:36:00.505 --> 00:36:00.925
SO,

00:36:01.144 --> 00:36:03.286
at the beginning of the concert season,

00:36:03.985 --> 00:36:07.688
We are installing an aluminium floor over the grass.

00:36:07.947 --> 00:36:08.268
So,

00:36:08.427 --> 00:36:09.128
the trucks,

00:36:09.148 --> 00:36:13.110
Cranes or trolleys can move freely to set up the concerts.

00:36:13.251 --> 00:36:15.072
Actually,

00:36:15.572 --> 00:36:16.851
We let the lawn die.

00:36:17.753 --> 00:36:19.354
But at the end of the concert season,

00:36:19.733 --> 00:36:23.276
The floor is removed and a brand new one is installed.

00:36:27.827 --> 00:36:31.209
While the Dutch are world-renowned for their vast tulip fields,

00:36:31.849 --> 00:36:34.010
They also have a perfect command of turf cultivation.

00:36:40.472 --> 00:36:41.673
We are in Eithwiesen.

00:36:42.293 --> 00:36:44.755
140 km from the Johan Cruyff Arena.

00:36:46.675 --> 00:36:49.777
This is where the future pitch of the stadium is being prepared.

00:36:51.858 --> 00:36:53.818
A lawn of a rather unusual kind.

00:36:54.659 --> 00:36:55.739
A hybrid lawn.

00:37:09.076 --> 00:37:14.394
Yves Decocker is the sales director for this lawn reinforced with a synthetic membrane.

00:37:22.976 --> 00:37:24.697
This synthetic fabric,

00:37:24.876 --> 00:37:25.837
this membrane,

00:37:25.857 --> 00:37:28.898
We are going to inject artificial fibers.

00:37:29.118 --> 00:37:32.300
Then we cover everything with custom-made sand.

00:37:32.340 --> 00:37:35.442
of a very specific particle size.

00:37:35.502 --> 00:37:36.982
It should not be too thick,

00:37:37.002 --> 00:37:38.223
not too crude,

00:37:38.224 --> 00:37:39.284
Not too thin either.

00:37:39.704 --> 00:37:41.005
It has to be absolutely perfect.

00:37:41.505 --> 00:37:43.406
And on top of these 30 mm of sand,

00:37:43.666 --> 00:37:45.047
we sow the grass.

00:37:47.819 --> 00:37:52.180
The hybrid lawn consists of a layer of polypropylene plastic fabric,

00:37:53.381 --> 00:37:58.422
onto which 6 cm long artificial polyethylene fibers are injected,

00:37:58.903 --> 00:38:00.343
in order to strengthen the structure.

00:38:04.684 --> 00:38:12.067
These fibers are fixed by a polyurethane spray which waterproofs the carpet and makes it insensitive to climate change.

00:38:14.235 --> 00:38:17.838
A 4cm layer of sand is placed on top of the synthetic fibers.

00:38:19.239 --> 00:38:22.221
From this specific sand and the sown seeds,

00:38:22.902 --> 00:38:28.045
The grass develops strong roots that will grow into the sand and become entangled in the carpet.

00:38:30.467 --> 00:38:31.768
After 3 to 4 months,

00:38:32.288 --> 00:38:37.512
when the natural grass is sufficiently dense and reaches a little over 2 cm in thickness above the sand,

00:38:38.213 --> 00:38:40.174
The turf is then ready to be delivered.

00:38:45.471 --> 00:38:46.311
But how to collect the sample?

00:38:46.532 --> 00:38:49.953
transporting and installing an entire lawn in just a few hours?

00:38:51.194 --> 00:38:54.036
The solution was conceived in 1997.

00:38:54.576 --> 00:38:56.116
one year after the stadium opened.

00:39:01.118 --> 00:39:08.342
We used all our creativity and invented our own technique for regrowing grass.

00:39:08.542 --> 00:39:10.723
These are rolls of turf, 5 cm thick.

00:39:11.344 --> 00:39:13.044
one meter wide and 8 meters long,

00:39:13.364 --> 00:39:14.024
large rolls.

00:39:14.725 --> 00:39:15.185
He pissed me off.

00:39:15.266 --> 00:39:17.067
develop a specific cutting machine,

00:39:17.427 --> 00:39:20.530
work with farmers to cultivate these patches properly.

00:39:20.970 --> 00:39:22.351
This was our first innovation,

00:39:23.072 --> 00:39:26.153
Rolled turf to replace the field in record time.

00:39:28.056 --> 00:39:28.396
Today,

00:39:28.476 --> 00:39:32.398
This technique has proven itself and is used in many parliamentary stadiums.

00:39:41.152 --> 00:39:45.153
No fewer than 25 trucks are needed to transport more than 300 rolls of vibrated air.

00:39:49.376 --> 00:39:58.159
50 people will work tirelessly to prepare and level the ground before covering the 7500 m² of the stadium with these large plots of grass.

00:40:11.483 --> 00:40:12.923
A veritable giant patchwork

00:40:13.244 --> 00:40:16.264
where the grass panels are directly opposite each other,

00:40:16.605 --> 00:40:17.665
no glue or sewing required.

00:40:22.746 --> 00:40:24.927
The weight of the panels is sufficient to hold them in place.

00:40:26.268 --> 00:40:31.829
Only 14 hours will have passed between the delivery of the rolls and the handover of a brand new pitch,

00:40:32.309 --> 00:40:33.770
ready to host the next match.

00:40:44.344 --> 00:40:48.166
Hybrid turf raises many questions.

00:40:48.686 --> 00:40:49.626
A hybrid lawn,

00:40:49.686 --> 00:40:52.269
Does that mean we're playing on artificial turf?

00:40:52.329 --> 00:40:52.729
No.

00:40:52.909 --> 00:40:56.791
And I want to be very clear on this point.

00:40:57.012 --> 00:40:58.592
Playing on a hybrid grass surface,

00:40:58.833 --> 00:41:02.155
It's like playing on natural grass.

00:41:02.175 --> 00:41:02.894
The trick,

00:41:03.015 --> 00:41:11.079
This is because synthetic fabrics and fibers are actually always below the level of natural grass.

00:41:11.344 --> 00:41:11.483
So,

00:41:11.604 --> 00:41:16.867
even when you play on it or touch it,

00:41:17.068 --> 00:41:19.911
you will be in contact with natural grass.

00:41:19.951 --> 00:41:25.434
The synthetic part of it is always located under the mowing surface.

00:41:25.815 --> 00:41:27.735
So you're playing on real grass.

00:41:27.976 --> 00:41:30.719
You will have natural playing conditions.

00:41:30.759 --> 00:41:36.222
It's natural grass reinforced with synthetic fibers that you can't see or feel.

00:41:42.331 --> 00:41:43.393
Thanks to the reinforced turf,

00:41:44.192 --> 00:41:48.757
The pitch can last a whole football season without suffering serious damage.

00:41:50.659 --> 00:41:51.578
But natural grass,

00:41:51.719 --> 00:41:51.920
She,

00:41:52.239 --> 00:41:53.480
needs regular care.

00:41:54.942 --> 00:41:55.581
Again,

00:41:56.063 --> 00:42:02.288
The stadium managers have innovated and proposed a system capable of monitoring the health of the pitch in real time.

00:42:10.842 --> 00:42:13.442
The grass is the most sensitive element of our stadium,

00:42:13.462 --> 00:42:16.545
because we want to offer Ajax players the very best in terms of pitch.

00:42:16.885 --> 00:42:19.867
For that,

00:42:19.887 --> 00:42:23.210
We have equipped ourselves with a system that allows us to control the quality of the ground.

00:42:24.449 --> 00:42:27.891
It notably consists of 15 sensors placed under the turf,

00:42:28.591 --> 00:42:33.213
distributed across the entire surface of the lawn and which constantly measure the temperature,

00:42:33.613 --> 00:42:37.794
humidity and the amount of light received by the grass.

00:42:43.959 --> 00:42:48.182
We also have a sensor installed behind the lawnmowers.

00:42:48.342 --> 00:42:58.309
These devices record data at the time of mowing that measures the vitality and density of the grass.

00:42:59.269 --> 00:43:03.952
This information allows us to know precisely the condition of the lawn.

00:43:04.112 --> 00:43:04.893
Is she doing well?

00:43:06.173 --> 00:43:07.054
Is she in good health?

00:43:08.115 --> 00:43:12.737
Or does it have deficiencies in fertilizer or light?

00:43:17.318 --> 00:43:18.599
With a 3.0 lawn,

00:43:19.420 --> 00:43:24.923
The teams in charge of maintenance have a wealth of data that helps them make the right decisions.

00:43:28.503 --> 00:43:35.773
can know precisely when and where more water or more light is needed to accelerate air regrowth.

00:43:39.237 --> 00:43:41.800
The data collected also allows us to anticipate the future.

00:43:46.487 --> 00:43:50.109
At the strategic level,

00:43:50.330 --> 00:43:53.132
We can say that if it's too matte,

00:43:53.452 --> 00:43:57.154
We can predict how long the grass will need to rest.

00:43:57.275 --> 00:43:59.156
So,

00:43:59.217 --> 00:44:01.097
Maintenance operations are necessary.

00:44:02.057 --> 00:44:10.760
This allows us to anticipate how the quality of the lawn will change over time.

00:44:10.861 --> 00:44:15.343
This allows us to better organize our interventions.

00:44:15.383 --> 00:44:25.887
And it also allows Ajax players to know how the matches have damaged the pitch and what conditions they will be playing in during the next matches.

00:44:29.976 --> 00:44:31.336
From the 2010s onwards,

00:44:31.958 --> 00:44:33.740
The leaders have set themselves another challenge.

00:44:34.701 --> 00:44:38.164
To make the Johan Cruyff Arena a showcase for sustainable development.

00:44:39.606 --> 00:44:43.410
The engineers had to revise their design in order to improve energy consumption.

00:44:44.411 --> 00:44:44.731
The goal?

00:44:45.432 --> 00:44:49.356
Use less fossil fuel in favor of more modern and sustainable sources.

00:44:58.599 --> 00:45:00.000
7000 m² of panels are...

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:02.400
Solar panels were thus installed all around the roof,

00:45:02.922 --> 00:45:13.487
the equivalent of the surface area of ​​a fleet's field.

00:45:13.827 --> 00:45:15.788
We produce 10%

00:45:16.188 --> 00:45:21.150
of our energy thanks to our solar panels.

00:45:21.831 --> 00:45:22.972
The other 90%

00:45:23.431 --> 00:45:26.193
come from wind turbines located about 30 km from here.

00:45:26.893 --> 00:45:30.476
30 km from here.

00:45:30.496 --> 00:45:30.996
Thanks to all of this,

00:45:31.317 --> 00:45:38.862
We therefore use entirely green electricity to be able to manage all of our facilities.

00:45:38.862 --> 00:45:42.565
It turned out that these solar panels were generating far more energy than needed.

00:45:43.284 --> 00:45:43.726
But alas,

00:45:43.786 --> 00:45:46.406
in times when we didn't need it.

00:45:46.768 --> 00:45:48.188
The sun shines during the day,

00:45:48.788 --> 00:45:51.990
while the matches and events take place in the evening.

00:45:52.030 --> 00:45:53.051
So we thought...

00:45:53.867 --> 00:45:57.871
Something is missing from our system.

00:45:57.873 --> 00:46:02.395
We need to be able to store solar energy.

00:46:04.577 --> 00:46:05.918
After two years of development,

00:46:06.219 --> 00:46:08.420
in partnership with a car manufacturer,

00:46:08.860 --> 00:46:10.202
The solution has finally been found.

00:46:12.143 --> 00:46:15.306
The surplus electricity will be stored in car batteries.

00:46:21.884 --> 00:46:27.548
The Arena's storage room is currently equipped with 148 new batteries or batteries from used vehicles.

00:46:29.411 --> 00:46:33.994
These batteries are connected to the electricity grid via 4 bidirectional converters.

00:46:36.077 --> 00:46:37.719
When they are powered and charged at

00:46:38.059 --> 00:46:41.902
100%, the batteries can store up to 3 MW of electricity.

00:46:43.003 --> 00:46:46.987
Enough to provide sufficient energy during matches or in case of a power outage.

00:46:49.148 --> 00:46:50.890
Aside from competitions and concerts,

00:46:51.930 --> 00:46:56.855
The energy stored in the batteries is also used to power the public grid during peak consumption periods.

00:46:58.776 --> 00:47:08.565
The electricity is then redistributed via the converter which transforms the direct current coming out of the batteries into alternating current used on the public electricity grid.

00:47:13.028 --> 00:47:15.591
The storage room is monitored 24 hours a day.

00:47:16.592 --> 00:47:17.553
In case of overheating,

00:47:18.093 --> 00:47:19.454
The team is ready to intervene.

00:47:21.375 --> 00:47:27.260
It is also necessary to ensure that the electricity supplied by the stadium complies with the public network distribution standards.

00:47:36.126 --> 00:47:37.007
What you see here,

00:47:37.327 --> 00:47:42.731
This is the bandwidth on which we agreed on the frequency with the network operator.

00:47:45.496 --> 00:47:45.797
Actually,

00:47:45.836 --> 00:47:50.759
The battery ensures that this frequency remains within the bandwidth.

00:47:51.400 --> 00:47:54.061
So if demand and usage vary greatly,

00:47:54.762 --> 00:47:57.262
The battery ensures it stays within this bandwidth.

00:47:57.503 --> 00:47:59.023
that is to say, within the 50 Hz range.

00:48:01.844 --> 00:48:05.628
Engineers have also found other alternative energy sources.

00:48:07.155 --> 00:48:07.396
So,

00:48:07.956 --> 00:48:14.898
The changing rooms and offices are now cooled by drawing cold water from the bottom of a lake located near the stadium.

00:48:16.639 --> 00:48:18.700
The warm water is then discharged back into the lake.

00:48:25.481 --> 00:48:26.742
The stadium escalators,

00:48:26.882 --> 00:48:27.822
coupled to a dynamo,

00:48:28.262 --> 00:48:31.324
produce electricity which is in turn sent to the grid.

00:48:35.260 --> 00:48:37.823
Thanks to these technologies distributed throughout the stadium,

00:48:38.303 --> 00:48:42.928
The Johan Cruyff Arena managed to achieve a zero carbon footprint as early as 2015.

00:48:43.709 --> 00:48:46.692
This makes it one of the most modern stadiums in the world today.

00:48:56.135 --> 00:49:01.680
People from all over the world came to admire what is now called the fifth generation of the football stadium.

00:49:03.401 --> 00:49:05.523
We are pioneers in this technology.

00:49:06.202 --> 00:49:10.465
And when they asked UEFA or FIFA where to find inspiration,

00:49:10.505 --> 00:49:11.166
they replied

00:49:11.847 --> 00:49:12.568
"Go to Amsterdam,

00:49:12.968 --> 00:49:13.889
"This is the stadium of the future."

00:49:18.012 --> 00:49:18.552
For his part,

00:49:19.351 --> 00:49:23.474
Parken Stadium proves to the world that such a venue can diversify.

00:49:29.748 --> 00:49:31.849
At the same time,

00:49:31.850 --> 00:49:33.110
This offers a significant advantage.

00:49:33.150 --> 00:49:40.355
That's because there's life in the stadium practically at all hours of the day and every day of the week.

00:49:40.615 --> 00:49:44.278
It does not remain unused like many stadiums that only experience a peak in activity.

00:49:44.657 --> 00:49:46.579
once a week when there is a football match,

00:49:47.278 --> 00:49:53.021
or only a few times a week.

00:49:53.661 --> 00:49:55.701
We wanted it to be a living, breathing house.

00:49:56.503 --> 00:49:59.304
a house that offers services to city dwellers in this neighborhood,

00:49:59.543 --> 00:50:00.443
here in Osterau,

00:50:00.983 --> 00:50:03.264
in Copenhagen and throughout Denmark.

00:50:07.106 --> 00:50:09.228
Two stadiums with different architecture.

00:50:10.427 --> 00:50:16.592
But two stadiums that have managed to preserve the spirit of sport while offering the public new experiences.

00:50:17.893 --> 00:50:21.815
Football temples transformed into veritable arenas where services,

00:50:22.056 --> 00:50:22.657
innovation,

00:50:22.916 --> 00:50:23.617
hospitality,

00:50:23.998 --> 00:50:26.219
Quality has become the new value.

00:50:27.340 --> 00:50:30.163
The values ​​of these 21st-century cathedrals.

